# usb_modeswitch dispatcher config for the Realtek RTL8188GU / RTL8710BU
# USB WiFi 6 adapter (ASUS USB-BE92 and other OEM shells of the same chip).
#
# Out of the box this adapter enumerates as a virtual SCSI CD-ROM with
# VID:PID 0bda:1a2b ("Realtek Semiconductor Corp. RTL8188GU 802.11n WLAN
# Adapter (Driver CDROM Mode)") containing Windows driver installers.
# After the modeswitch the same USB device flips its product ID to
# 0bda:b711 and exposes the vendor-specific WLAN interface that the
# mainline rtl8xxxu driver (drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8xxxu/8710b.c)
# matches with USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(USB_VENDOR_ID_REALTEK, 0xb711,...).
#
# IMPORTANT: this switch is a USB control-message modeswitch, NOT a SCSI
# eject. The kernel's unusual_devs.h (entry at lines ~1509 in the 6.8
# source, "Reported by Zenm Chen") deliberately marks 0bda:1a2b with
# US_FL_IGNORE_DEVICE so that the usb-storage driver refuses to bind the
# autoinstall-CD interface — the kernel log will report:
#     usb-storage 1-X:1.0: USB Mass Storage device detected
#     usb-storage 1-X:1.0: device ignored
# and there will be NO /dev/sr0 to `eject`. The IGNORE is intentional so
# that usb_modeswitch (rather than the kernel's cdrom plymount) can drive
# the flip. The comment in unusual_devs.h is explicit:
#   "Ignore driver CD mode, otherwise usb_modeswitch may fail to switch
#    the device into Wi-Fi mode."
#
# Because usb-storage never binds, DetachStorageOnly=1 (the cdrom-eject
# shortcut used for many Realtek autoinstall-CD chips on distros where
# usb-storage *does* bind) does nothing here. Instead usb_modeswitch must
# speak USB Mass Storage Bulk-Only Transport directly to the device and
# send it a SCSI START_STOP_UNIT (opcode 0x1b) with LoEJ=1 (load/eject
# the medium), which Realtek's firmware interprets as "exit the
# autoinstall-CD persona and re-enumerate as a WLAN adapter".
#
# The MessageContent below is the 31-byte Command Block Wrapper (CBW)
# for START_STOP_UNIT:
#   55 53 42 43          CBW signature
#   12 34 56 78          tag
#   00 00 00 00          data transfer length (no data phase)
#   00                   flags (host->device, OUT)
#   06                   LUN
#   06                   CDB length
#   1b                   SCSI START_STOP_UNIT opcode
#   00                   immediate=0
#   00 00                reserved
#   02                   start=0, load/eject=1 (LoEJ=1)
#   00                   power condition 0
#   00 00 ... 00         pad to 31 bytes
#
# Stock usb_modeswitch-data does NOT ship an entry for 0bda:1a2b — this
# file is the only thing that makes the auto-switch happen on a minimal
# Yocto demo-image-base build.
#
# Install path: /etc/usb_modeswitch.d/0bda:1a2b (the usb_modeswitch udev
# dispatcher at /lib/udev/usb_modeswitch picks it up by filename).
DefaultVendor=0x0bda
DefaultProduct=0x1a2b
TargetVendor=0x0bda
TargetProduct=0xb711
MessageContent="5553424312345678000000000000061b000000020000000000000000000000"
CheckSuccess=20
